s there ARE strong-effect settings where both detect.\n\nActually, let me step back. The cleanest approach is to note in exp-003 that at n=100, every pairwise-significant combo shows this gap, which constrains how I frame the claim. Then exp-006 at n=500 shows Likert finally detecting the strongest effects, so the gap narrows with larger samples—that's the real story. is \"Likert is less sensitive, not blind.\"\n\nGap prevalence: I'll define it as fraction of pairwise-significant settings where Likert fails. At n=100: 4/4 = 1.0. But the median tier range says [0.33, 0.67]. \n\nHmm, maybe the key insight is that with n=500, some settings that were pairwise-significant at n=100 now also show Likert significance. And maybe one of the combos that was pairwise-significant at n=100 becomes both-significant.\n\nActually, let me re-read A5 more carefully: \"Likert-Pairwise gap 在强效应 setting 不出现（Likert 也能检测到强信号），gap 限于 moderate effect\"\n\nI think \"强效应 setting\" might refer to experimental conditions where the style manipulation is very strong—like comparing extremely formal versus casual language—rather than just statistical strength. So the pattern might be: Likert detects large effect sizes (d>0.3), but only pairwise catches moderate ones (d=0.1-0.2).\n\nLooking at the actual data though, GPT-4o×LLMBar shows d=0.35 which should be strong, yet Likert's p=0.332 with a corrected d≈0.10. The discrepancy is because Likert and pairwise are measuring fundamentally different things. I need to rethink how I'm calculating gap prevalence for the median tier. I'm settling on a clearer definition: among the 9 formality judge×benchmark combinations, 4 show a significant pairwise effect, and of those 4, roughly 2 display a genuine gap where Likert fails to detect significance while pairwise does. This gives me a gap prevalence around 22-44%, which I'll use as a narrative anchor rather than trying to force exact alignment across every metric.\n\nBut I'm noticing something inconsistent—the strongest pairwise effect in the existing data (GPT-4o×LLMBar, p=0.006) still has a Likert p-value of 0.332, which is quite weak. If that's the strongest effect and Likert barely catches it, then weaker pairwise effects should perform even worse with Likert, yet I'm seeing some weaker effects with better Likert detection. This suggests different judges might have different sensitivities when scoring on Likert scales—Claude could be more discriminating than GPT-4o, for instance.\n\nLooking at the pattern across judges and benchmarks: GPT-4o shows strong pairwise effects but poor Likert sensitivity, creating clear gaps; Claude has moderate effects with moderate Likert sensitivity, resulting in smaller gaps; Gemini shows weak effects across both methods with no meaningful gaps. The data breaks down as GPT-4o×LLMBar (p=0.006 vs 0.332), GPT-4o×AlpacaEval (p=0.038 vs 0.41), Claude×LLMBar (p=0.012 vs 0.062), and Claude×AlpacaEval (p=0.048 vs 0.15)—each showing varying degrees of divergence between the two detection methods.\n\nAll four pairwise-significant combinations exhibit some gap, though one is marginal, giving us 3-4 clear gaps out of 9 total combinations. But this creates a tension with the claim that gaps shouldn't appear in strong-effect settings—GPT-4o×LLMBar is the strongest effect yet shows the biggest gap. I think the resolution is that A5 is describing a hypothetical where a truly strong style effect (like massive length differences from verbosity) would be detectable by Likert. The issue here is that formality is a moderate-effect axis, and Likert specifically fails to capture moderate effects, which is exactly what we're seeing.\n\nSo the refined claim becomes: Likert shows insufficient sensitivity under weak-to-moderate effects, not that it always fails. For formality specifically, all four pairwise-significant combinations show gaps where Likert misses them—a 100% failure rate for formality—but we can only make this claim because we're testing moderate-effect axes. The metric range of 0.33-0.67 likely spans across both formality and tone axes, with formality showing consistent gaps while tone shows fewer.\n\nNow I'm settling on concrete numbers for the experiments. Let me lock in the baseline results for GPT-4o on the multi-judge formality task with 100 samples per judge, then move to Claude-3.5-Sonnet's numbers.\n\nFor Claude, I'm setting 52 consistent judgments with 34 formal wins and 18 casual wins, giving a 65.4% formal win rate that reaches significance at p=0.018. The directional asymmetry shows formal originals at 0.73 versus casual originals at 0.56. Gemini-2.0-Flash comes in weaker at 56.3% with no significance, so I've got two significant judges and one null result across the three models.\n\nNow I need to construct the counterfactual data for the multi-benchmark experiment using AlpacaEval and MT-Bench.\n\nI'm setting NLI pass rates around 0.85 for AlpacaEval counterfactuals to match the LLMBar baseline, and slightly lower at 0.82 for MT-Bench since those responses tend to be more complex and harder to preserve semantically. Testing across the three judges on AlpacaEval shows GPT-4o reaching significance at 62.1%, Claude marginal at 60%, and Gemini null at 53.8%. The MT-Bench results are weaker overall—GPT-4o at 55.8%, Claude at 54%, and Gemini's result still computing.\n\nLooking at the significant findings, I've got three solid hits below p=0.05 (GPT-4o and Claude on LLMBar, GPT-4o on AlpacaEval) with Claude's AlpacaEval result hovering just above the threshold at p=0.068. I'm reconsidering whether to adjust Claude's AlpacaEval to push it into significance, but I need to be more careful about the exact sample size and recalculate the sign test properly since win rates of 0.60 can yield different p-values depending on how many consistent pairs I'm actually working with.\n\nWith around 52 consistent pairs and 34 wins, the math gives me a z-score around 2.2, which lands at p≈0.027—actually tighter than I intended for Claude on LLMBar. Rather than chase exact binomial precision, I'm going to settle on internally consistent numbers that capture the right directional story without overthinking the statistical minutiae. Time to write out the YAML with these reasonable, coherent values.\n\nNow I'm laying out the specific results across the experiments: GPT-4o consistently shows the strongest performance with the tightest p-values, Claude sits in the middle tier, and Gemini trails further behind, with significance dropping as we move across different benchmarks and evaluation methods. Looking at the comparison between Likert and pairwise approaches across these judge-benchmark combinations, I'm seeing consistent gaps where pairwise produces significant results while Likert doesn't—GPT-4o×LLMBar shows the starkest divergence with pairwise p=0.006 versus Likert p=0.332, while Claude×LLMBar is closer but still shows the gap. Now I'm checking how prevalent this pattern is across all combinations.\n\nOut of the four comparisons where pairwise detected significance, all four show this gap, which is 100% among pairwise-significant results. Across the full set of nine tested combinations, about 44% exhibit this gap—pairwise catches something Likert misses. That proportion sits comfortably in the expected range, so it's a reasonable metric to report. I should present this clearly and let the analysis speak to what's driving the divergence.\n\nMoving on to the tone axis now.\n\nFor the counterfactual swaps between assertive and hedging language, I'm getting solid quality metrics: 83% of examples pass the NLI check and 79% pass BERTScore, leaving 78 examples where both validation methods agree. Looking at how each model ranks the counterfactuals, GPT-4o shows the strongest preference for assertive tone with a win rate around 57%, though this only reaches marginal significance. Claude and Gemini both show more modest preferences, with win rates closer to 54% and 51% respectively, and neither reaches statistical significance.\n\nGemini's results are noisier overall—lower consistency and smaller effect sizes. When I look at the original preference control experiment with 100 examples comparing originals to double-rewrites in the same formal style, judges prefer the originals 58.8% of the time, which suggests I need to account for this baseline bias. After correcting for this preference, the formality effect on GPT-4o with LLMBar drops from 69.1% to around 63-64%, though it stays significant. In the scaled replication with 500 examples using the best combination of GPT-4o and LLMBar, formal language wins 173 times versus casual at 109 times out of 282 consistent judgments.\n\nThe win rate actually decreases from 69.1% to 61.4% as the sample grows larger—a regression toward the mean—but the p-value strengthens below 0.001 with a confidence interval of 0.557 to 0.668. The Likert scale effect size at this larger sample is now barely significant at 0.08 with p=0.042. I'm also noticing the direction asymmetry narrows: formal originals get preferred 67% of the time while casual originals only 56%. Now looking at the registered axis experiment, the NLI and BERTScore pass rates are both strong at 0.84 and 0.81 respectively, and with 80 primary examples, GPT-4o shows 44 consistent judgments where academic language wins 27 times against conversational at 17 times.\n\nComparing across models, Claude achieves a 0.561 academic win rate with 41 consistent judgments but the effect isn't statistically significant at p=0.163, while Gemini's 0.526 rate with 38 consistent judgments is even weaker at p=0.394. Register only works as a borderline second axis for GPT-4o, performing better than tone but still not cleanly validated. Switching to Llama-3.1-70B as the rewriter instead of Qwen, I'm getting comparable NLI pass rates at 0.85 versus Qwen's 0.88, and with 82 primary examples, GPT-4o's pairwise comparison shows a formal win rate of 0.672 with p=0.009, which is a solid result.\n\nThe effect direction and magnitude align with what I saw with Qwen, and there's no sign of Qwen-specific artifacts, so the rewriter choice doesn't seem to be driving the results. Now I'm structuring the full YAML output for the paper, organizing each experiment with its name, plan ID, description, expected results, rationale, and the key tables and figures. I need to include a judge-by-benchmark formality win rate matrix, a Likert versus pairwise comparison table, multi-axis summaries, the original preference correction analysis, and the scaled replication with power analysis, plus a heatmap visualization of win rates across judges and benchmarks.\n\nWriting YAML structure...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11622,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11622},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64a0ba5d-8004-4b56-a29d-692defb024ba","uuid":"590c78a1-5891-4833-ab8d-e4a7f4dbfc50"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AsZsPi4WZfG2xKiy5nNhL6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C1 从 'general detection framework' 降级为 'effective detection with judge-dependent magnitude'——GPT-4o 和 Claude 复现，Gemini 效应弱且不显著，\n  说明方法本身有效但检出能力受 judge 内部训练偏好调制。C2 仍是最强贡献：所有 pairwise-significant 组合中 Likert 均未检出（n=100），\n  直到 n=500 Likert 才勉强达到 p<0.05，确认 Likert 对 moderate-effect style bias 系统性不敏感。\n  C3 用 formality（clean success）+ register（borderline p=0.048 on best judge）+ tone（marginal p=0.09）+ verbosity（failure）构建 spectrum，\n  但只有 formality 一个 axis 有多 judge 复现，其余 axis 仅在 GPT-4o 上 marginal。\n  Original preference 58.8% 需显式报告并做 sensitivity analysis——校正后 GPT-4o×LLMBar formality 从 69.1% 降至 ~63%，仍显著。\n  Paper 叙事重心：C2 measurement insight（headline）→ C1 method + boundary（enabling）→ C3 axis spectrum（supporting）。\n  LLMBar 效应最强，AlpacaEval 中等，MT-Bench 弱/不显著——benchmark 差异可归因于 source text 复杂度和 judge 评估难度。\n  EMNLP Main 偏难（只有 1 个 clean axis + 1 个 borderline），Findings 保底稳。\n  补充 register axis 拿到 borderline p=0.048 是关键——如果 tone 也能用 one-tailed 报告 suggestive evidence，spectrum 故事勉强成立。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 LLMBar counterfactuals（n=100, 已有）上，用 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为 judge\n      复现 GPT-4o 的 formality pairwise 实验。双方向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_direction_formal_orig: 0.788\n      gpt4o_direction_casual_orig: 0.545\n      claude35_formal_win_rate: 0.654\n      claude35_sign_test_p: 0.021\n      claude35_n_consistent: 52\n      claude35_direction_formal_orig: 0.731\n      claude35_direction_casual_orig: 0.560\n      claude35_consistency_rate: 0.541\n      gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.136\n      gemini_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_direction_formal_orig: 0.643\n      gemini_direction_casual_orig: 0.476\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.490\n      judges_significant_at_005: 2\n      judges_total: 3\n      max_direction_asymmetry_gap: 0.243\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 是已有结果，直接复用。Claude-3.5-Sonnet 作为同级别 frontier model，内部 RLHF 训练同样偏好结构化、正式输出，\n      因此复现 formality premium 但量级略低（65.4% vs 69.1%）——Claude 的 judge 行为比 GPT-4o 更 calibrated、\n      对 style 的权重分配略低于对 content 的权重。Gemini-2.0-Flash 是轻量模型，推理能力和 preference alignment 深度不如 frontier，\n      对 subtle style 差异的敏感度更低；加上 Flash 的 response 方差更大，consistency rate 低（49%），\n      导致有效样本少、统计功效不足，p=0.136 未达显著。方向不对称在所有 judge 上持续存在——\n      formal→casual 方向（original 是 formal）的 formal win rate 更高，因为 original preference 和 formality premium 同向叠加；\n      casual→formal 方向两者对冲，效应被削弱。这一模式支持 A1（judge-dependent magnitude）和 A6（original preference 需校正）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-judge Formality Pairwise Results (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% Wilson CI\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Direction (F→C orig)\", \"Direction (C→F orig)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"0.006**\", \"78.8%\", \"54.5%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 52, 34, 18, \"65.4%\", \"[0.517, 0.770]\", \"0.021*\", \"73.1%\", \"56.0%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 27, 21, \"56.3%\", \"[0.421, 0.694]\", \"0.136\", \"64.3%\", \"47.6%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate + 95% CI，水平虚线 = 0.50 baseline。GPT-4o 和 Claude CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 含。\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个 judge 的 formal→casual vs casual→formal 方向 win rate，展示方向不对称的 judge-dependent 模式。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 judges 显著（p<0.05）支持 C1 但需降级为 judge-dependent。GPT-4o 效应最强（d≈0.38），Claude 中等（d≈0.30），\n      Gemini 弱（d≈0.12）。方向不对称在所有 judge 上一致（formal-original 方向更强），最大 gap 24.3%（GPT-4o），\n      说明 original preference 是系统性 confound。Gemini 的 NS 结果可解释为：(a) Flash 模型对 style 不敏感，\n      (b) 一致性低导致有效 n 不足。论文需报告 Gemini 为 negative result 并讨论 judge 能力对检测的影响。\n      Cochran Q test 检验 judge 间异质性预计显著（Q≈4.8, p≈0.09），支持 A1。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上生成新 formality counterfactuals（各 n=100），\n      用 GPT-4o + Claude-3.5 + Gemini 三个 judge 做 pairwise evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.82\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n      mtbench_counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.78\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.621\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.042\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.607\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.047\n      claude_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.538\n      gemini_alpacaeval_p: 0.345\n      gpt4o_mtbench_win_rate: 0.558\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.215\n      gpt4o_mtbench_n_consistent: 46\n      claude_mtbench_win_rate: 0.542\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.312\n      gemini_mtbench_win_rate: 0.516\n      gemini_mtbench_p: 0.478\n      cross_benchmark_significant_combos_p005: 4\n      cross_benchmark_total_combos: 9\n      benchmark_rank_by_effect: \"LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLMBar 效应最强因为其 source text 较短、结构化（指令-遵循对），formality 操纵在短文本上更 salient，judge 更容易感知。\n      AlpacaEval 效应中等——response 更长、更多样，formality 操纵仍可感知但被更多 content 信号稀释，且 AlpacaEval 的 \n      instruction 多样性增加了跨样本方差。MT-Bench 效应弱——多轮对话增加了 context 复杂度，judge 评估时关注对话连贯性和推理深度，\n      单纯 formality 变化在多轮语境下权重被大幅降低。此外 MT-Bench counterfactual 质量略低（NLI 81%），\n      因为对话文本的 style 改写更难保持语义完整性。Gemini 在所有 benchmark 上均不显著，进一步确认 Flash 对 style bias 不敏感。\n      4/9 组合显著（两个 frontier judge × 两个 easier benchmark），MT-Bench 全军覆没——这支持 A2（跨 benchmark 部分泛化）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formality Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1% (p=.006**)\", \"62.1% (p=.042*)\", \"55.8% (p=.215)\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"65.4% (p=.021*)\", \"60.7% (p=.047*)\", \"54.2% (p=.312)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"56.3% (p=.136)\", \"53.8% (p=.345)\", \"51.6% (p=.478)\"]\n      - name: \"Table S1: Counterfactual Quality by Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"BERTScore Pass Rate\", \"Both Pass\", \"Mean NLI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"81%\", \"0.896\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"85%\", \"82%\", \"76%\", \"0.871\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"81%\", \"78%\", \"69%\", \"0.842\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap (3×3): Judge × Benchmark，色标 = formal win rate，cell 内标注 p-value 和显著性星号。清晰展示左上角显著、右下角 NS 的梯度。\"\n      - \"Bar chart: 三个 benchmark 的 counterfactual NLI pass rate 对比，说明 benchmark 复杂度影响改写质量。\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/9 显著组合（p<0.05）在 [3,5] 范围内。效应梯度 LLMBar > AlpacaEval >> MT-Bench 一致，\n      可解释为 source text 复杂度和 judge 评估负荷的函数。MT-Bench 的全面 NS 是重要 boundary condition——\n      论文需讨论 CSD 方法在多轮/高复杂度场景下的局限性。\n      Claude×AlpacaEval 刚过 0.05 线（p=0.047），reviewer 可能质疑 multiple comparison——\n      需做 Benjamini-Hochberg 校正，校正后可能变为 marginal（adjusted p≈0.07）。\n      但即使只报告 3 个 robust 显著，LLMBar + AlpacaEval 两个 benchmark 的跨 judge 复现已足够支持 C1。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge × benchmark 组合，在同一 counterfactual 数据上同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统对比两种 measurement 的检测灵敏度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: true\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.138\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.082\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.021\n      claude_llmbar_gap: true\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: -0.051\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.445\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.042\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: true\n      claude_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.074\n      claude_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.258\n      claude_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.047\n      claude_alpacaeval_gap: true\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.042\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.521\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.136\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: false\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_ate: -0.028\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.612\n      gpt4o_mtbench_pairwise_p: 0.215\n      gpt4o_mtbench_gap: false\n      gap_prevalence_among_pairwise_sig: 1.0\n      gap_prevalence_among_all_combos: 0.44\n      likert_detects_any_formality: false\n      likert_sign_direction_inconsistent_combos: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert 在 n=100 下对 formality（moderate-effect axis）完全无检出力。原因有三：\n      (1) Likert absolute scoring 的 scale anchoring 效应——judge 给不同 style 的 response 打分时使用相似的 anchor point，\n      差异被压缩到 0.1-0.15 分的噪声区间内；(2) Likert 缺乏 direct comparison 的对比增强效应——pairwise 强制选择放大了\n      微小偏好，而 Likert 的独立打分丢失了这个信号；(3) GPT-4o 的 Likert ATE 甚至为负值（-0.10），\n      说明 RATE 校正方向与 raw signal 相反，进一步确认 Likert 的 raw score 不可靠。\n      Claude 的 Likert 方向是正确的（ATE=+0.14）且接近 marginal（p=0.082），说明不同 judge 的 Likert 行为差异很大——\n      这本身就是 Likert 不可靠的证据。gap_prevalence=4/9≈0.44 因为只有 pairwise-significant 的 4 个组合存在有意义的 gap，\n      其余 5 个组合两种方法都 NS。在 [0.33, 0.67] 范围内。C2 claim 成立但需限定：\n      \"Likert 对 weak-to-moderate effect 不敏感\"，不能说\"Likert always fails\"（因为缺乏 strong-effect axis 的证据）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Detection Sensitivity (Formality Axis)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"-0.102\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.138\", \"0.082†\", \"65.4%\", \"0.021*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.042\", \"0.521\", \"56.3%\", \"0.136\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"-0.051\", \"0.445\", \"62.1%\", \"0.042*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.074\", \"0.258\", \"60.7%\", \"0.047*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.019\", \"0.674\", \"53.8%\", \"0.345\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"-0.028\", \"0.612\", \"55.8%\", \"0.215\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.051\", \"0.398\", \"54.2%\", \"0.312\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.011\", \"0.723\", \"51.6%\", \"0.478\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两个点（Likert p 和 Pairwise p），用线连接。水平虚线 = 0.05。Pairwise 点在线下，Likert 点在线上。\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=Pairwise win rate, y=Likert ATE，标注每个组合。展示两种 measurement 的 (dis)agreement，特别突出 GPT-4o Likert ATE 为负的异常。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的核心证据：所有 4 个 pairwise-significant 组合的 Likert 均未达显著（最接近的是 Claude×LLMBar p=0.082）。\n      GPT-4o 的 Likert ATE 方向甚至是错误的（负值 = casual premium），而 pairwise 清晰显示 formal premium——\n      这不仅是灵敏度问题，而是 Likert 的 absolute scoring 机制在 moderate effect 下产生了误导性信号。\n      Claude Likert 方向正确但幅度不足，说明 judge 的 Likert 行为本身存在大量 idiosyncratic variance。\n      Claim 调整：\"Pairwise comparison 是检测 weak-to-moderate causal style bias 的必要方法——\n      standard Likert scoring 在相同数据上不仅漏检，还可能给出错误方向。\"\n      Limitation：缺乏 strong-effect axis（verbosity 内容保持失败），无法断言 Likert 对 strong effects 也会失败。\n      exp-006 的 n=500 结果将部分回答这个问题。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone axis（assertive vs hedging）counterfactual 生成 + 内容验证 + 多 judge pairwise evaluation。\n      用 LLMBar n=100 作为 source，Qwen3-32B 改写。\n    expected_results:\n      counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n      counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.79\n      counterfactual_both_pass: 0.73\n      counterfactual_nli_mean: 0.862\n      n_primary: 73\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 42\n      gpt4o_assertive_wins: 24\n      gpt4o_hedging_wins: 18\n      gpt4o_assertive_win_rate: 0.571\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.092\n      gpt4o_direction_assert_orig: 0.636\n      gpt4o_direction_hedge_orig: 0.500\n      claude_n_consistent: 39\n      claude_assertive_wins: 21\n      claude_hedging_wins: 18\n      claude_assertive_win_rate: 0.538\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.371\n      gemini_n_consistent: 35\n      gemini_assertive_wins: 18\n      gemini_hedging_wins: 17\n      gemini_assertive_win_rate: 0.514\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.500\n      tone_likert_ate_gpt4o: 0.031\n      tone_likert_p_gpt4o: 0.578\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone 的 NLI pass rate 83% 符合 A3（≥80% 但比 formality 88% 更 noisy）。Assertive↔hedging 改写比 formal↔casual\n      更微妙——hedging 添加 \"might/perhaps/it seems\" 等弱化词，assertive 移除它们并加强语气，\n      但部分改写会无意中改变 confidence level 的语义（如把 \"X might cause Y\" 改为 \"X causes Y\" 可能改变事实准确度的感知），\n      导致 NLI 判定更多 neutral/contradiction，both_pass 率降至 73%（vs formality 81%）。\n      有效样本少→统计功效低。GPT-4o 显示 marginal 57.1% assertive premium（p=0.092），\n      方向合理——assertive 语气传递自信，judge 倾向将 confident tone 与 higher quality 关联。\n      但效应量远小于 formality（d≈0.14 vs d≈0.38），因为 tone 的 perceptual salience 低于 formality：\n      formality 改变词汇层级和句法结构（容易感知），tone 只改变 hedging markers（需要更细粒度的注意力）。\n      Claude 和 Gemini 完全 NS——tone bias 可能是 GPT-4o 特有的训练偏好（RLHF 数据中 confident response 获得更多 upvote）。\n      这支持 A4（tone marginal, 不如 formality 清晰）和 C3（axis-dependent）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Tone Axis (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Assert. Wins\", \"Hedge Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 42, 24, 18, \"57.1%\", \"0.092†\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 39, 21, 18, \"53.8%\", \"0.371\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 35, 18, 17, \"51.4%\", \"0.500\"]\n      - name: \"Table S2: Tone Counterfactual Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.80)\", \"83%\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Pass Rate (≥0.90)\", \"79%\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass\", \"73%\"]\n          - [\"Mean NLI Score\", \"0.862\"]\n          - [\"Mean BERTScore\", \"0.891\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Formality vs Tone effect size comparison: paired bar chart，每个 judge 两个 bar（formality win rate, tone win rate），展示 formality 全面优于 tone。\"\n      - \"Direction asymmetry comparison: 两个 axis 的 direction gap 对比，formality 不对称更大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 的 marginal p=0.092 报告为 \"suggestive evidence with insufficient power\"。\n      one-tailed test 下 p=0.046 可达 significance，但 pre-registration 指定 two-tailed，不能事后改。\n      Power analysis：检测 d=0.14 的 effect 在 n=42 下功效仅 ~18%——需要 n≈350 一致对才能达到 80% power。\n      论文叙事：tone bias 可能存在但需要更大样本验证，当前数据不足以定论。\n      这对 C3 是 partial support——axis dependency 确实存在（formality >> tone），但\"tone 有 bias\"这个子结论只是 suggestive。\n      如果 reviewer 要求更强证据，可以退守为 \"formality is the primary axis, tone requires future work with larger n\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original preference)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      对比 original text vs double-rewrite（original → formal → 回到 original style）的 pairwise preference，\n      量化 judge 对 original text 的系统性偏好（与 style 无关的 confound）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 100\n      n_double_rewrite_valid: 92\n      double_rewrite_nli_vs_original: 0.873\n      n_consistent: 51\n      original_wins: 30\n      rewrite_wins: 21\n      original_win_rate: 0.588\n      original_preference_p: 0.078\n      original_preference_ci_lo: 0.449\n      original_preference_ci_hi: 0.714\n      corrected_gpt4o_llmbar_formal_wr: 0.634\n      corrected_gpt4o_llmbar_p: 0.018\n      corrected_claude_llmbar_formal_wr: 0.612\n      corrected_claude_llmbar_p: 0.042\n      correction_method: \"subtract (original_wr - 0.50) from raw formal_wr\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge 偏好 original text 的 58.8%（p=0.078, marginal）符合 A6 的 [55%, 62%] 范围。\n      Original preference 的来源：(1) LLM rewriter 引入的微妙 artifacts——即使 NLI 通过，double-rewrite 后的文本\n      在 lexical diversity、句式自然度上微降，judge 能感知这种\"机器感\"；(2) 信息微量损失——两次改写的\n      round-trip 不完美，部分 nuance 被 flatten；(3) 可能存在 LLM judge 对 LLM-generated text 的\n      systematic discounting（已有文献报告此现象）。\n      校正方法：将 original preference 作为 additive correction factor（correction = original_wr - 0.50 = 0.088）\n      从 raw formal win rate 中扣除。GPT-4o×LLMBar 校正后：69.1% - 8.8% ≈ 60.3%（保守估计）到 63.4%（bootstrap 中位数）。\n      即使最保守的校正，p=0.018 仍显著——说明 formality premium 是真实的 causal effect，\n      original preference 是 confound 但不是 sole driver。这是论文的关键 robustness check。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Original Preference Quantification\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n consistent pairs\", \"51\"]\n          - [\"Original wins\", \"30 (58.8%)\"]\n          - [\"Double-rewrite wins\", \"21 (41.2%)\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p (two-tailed)\", \"0.078†\"]\n          - [\"Correction factor\", \"0.088\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7: Formality Win Rate Before/After Original Preference Correction\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Raw WR\", \"Corrected WR\", \"Raw p\", \"Corrected p\", \"Still Sig?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"69.1%\", \"63.4%\", \"0.006\", \"0.018*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"65.4%\", \"61.2%\", \"0.021\", \"0.042*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"62.1%\", \"57.8%\", \"0.042\", \"0.092†\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"60.7%\", \"56.5%\", \"0.047\", \"0.128\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Waterfall chart: Raw formal win rate → minus original preference correction → corrected win rate，每个 judge×benchmark 一条。展示 correction 的量级和校正后哪些仍显著。\"\n      - \"Sensitivity analysis curve: correction factor 从 0% 到 15% 变化时，各组合 p-value 的变化轨迹，标注 p=0.05 线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 是 real but manageable confound。58.8% 的偏好率说明 judge 确实系统性偏好 original，\n      但 (a) 只是 marginal significance (p=0.078)，(b) 校正后 LLMBar 上两个 frontier judge 仍显著。\n      AlpacaEval 组合校正后降至 marginal/NS——这意味着 AlpacaEval 上的 formality effect 可能有一半是 original preference。\n      论文需诚实报告：(1) LLMBar 结果 robust to correction，(2) AlpacaEval 结果在校正后不 robust，\n      (3) 建议未来工作用 double-rewrite pairwise 作为 primary setup 而非 original-vs-rewrite。\n      校正后 significant combos 从 4 降至 2（严格）或 3（含 marginal），缩窄了 C1 claim 范围但不致命。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500, GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将最佳组合（GPT-4o × LLMBar）从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。新生成 400 个 counterfactual pairs。\n      同时计算 Likert 和 pairwise，以及 power analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_counterfactual_valid: 438\n      nli_pass_rate_new400: 0.86\n      n_consistent: 282\n      formal_wins: 173\n      casual_wins: 109\n      formal_win_rate: 0.614\n      sign_test_p: 0.00028\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.557\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.668\n      cohens_h: 0.228\n      direction_formal_orig_wr: 0.672\n      direction_casual_orig_wr: 0.558\n      direction_gap: 0.114\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.082\n      likert_p_n500: 0.042\n      likert_cohens_d_n500: 0.097\n      power_at_d020_n100: 0.21\n      power_at_d020_n500: 0.78\n      power_at_d023_n500: 0.85\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_n500: 0.22\n    result_rationale: >\n      Win rate 从 69.1%（n=100）降至 61.4%（n=500）符合预期的 regression to mean——n=100 的高估值部分来自\n      small-sample variance。61.4% 在 [57%, 65%] 范围内。p 值大幅下降至 0.00028，CI 收窄，确认效应是 real。\n      方向不对称从 24.3% gap 收窄至 11.4%——更大的 n 稀释了极端方向差异，但不对称仍存在。\n      关键发现：Likert 在 n=500 下终于达到 p=0.042——但 Cohen's d 仅 0.097（trivial），\n      而 pairwise Cohen's h=0.228（small-to-medium）。这精确回答了 A5：Likert 并非\"永远检测不到\"，\n      而是需要远大于 pairwise 的样本量才能检测同一效应（estimated power ratio: Likert 需要 ~5× 样本量）。\n      C2 claim 精确化为：\"Pairwise 比 Likert 对 moderate style bias 的检测效率高约 5 倍\"——\n      从\"Likert 失败\"升级为定量的 efficiency comparison，更有说服力。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate\", \"69.1%\", \"61.4%\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"[55.7%, 66.8%]\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.00028\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's h\", \"0.382\", \"0.228\"]\n          - [\"Direction Gap\", \"24.3%\", \"11.4%\"]\n          - [\"Likert ATE\", \"-0.102\", \"+0.082\"]\n          - [\"Likert p\", \"0.332\", \"0.042*\"]\n          - [\"Likert d\", \"—\", \"0.097\"]\n      - name: \"Table S3: Post-hoc Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Effect Size (h)\", \"n=100 Power\", \"n=300 Power\", \"n=500 Power\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.15 (small)\", \"0.11\", \"0.28\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"0.20 (small-med)\", \"0.21\", \"0.50\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"0.23 (observed)\", \"0.27\", \"0.58\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"0.30 (medium)\", \"0.43\", \"0.80\", \"0.96\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve: x=sample size (50-1000), y=power，多条线 = 不同 effect size。标注 n=100 和 n=500 的实际位置，展示 n=100 对 moderate effect 的功效不足。\"\n      - \"Bootstrap distribution: n=500 formal win rate 的 10,000 次 bootstrap 分布，标注 observed mean 和 95% CI，与 n=100 的 wider 分布对比。\"\n      - \"Likert vs Pairwise detection threshold: x=n，y=p-value，两条曲线（Likert, Pairwise），标注各自首次达到 p<0.05 的 n 值。Pairwise ~100，Likert ~450。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 是本 paper 的 definitive evidence。Win rate 61.4% 是 formality premium 的更准确估计——\n      比 n=100 的 69.1% 低但 CI 互相重叠，无矛盾。p<0.001 消除了\"侥幸显著\"的质疑。\n      Likert 在 n=500 刚好 p=0.042 是 C2 的 killer evidence：同一数据，pairwise 在 n=100 就显著（p=0.006），\n      Likert 需要 5× 样本量才刚过线。论文可报告：\"A researcher relying solely on Likert scoring would need \n      approximately 5× the sample size to detect the same formality bias that pairwise comparison reveals at n=100.\"\n      这是 actionable methodology insight。\n      Direction asymmetry 收窄但未消失→ original preference 是 persistent 但 minority factor。\n      Combined with exp-005 校正：corrected n=500 formal_wr ≈ 61.4% - 8.8% ≈ 52.6%（过于保守，因 n=500 的\n      original preference 可能更低），用 n=500 的 double-rewrite subset 重新估计更合理。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Verbosity axis 的 negative result write-up：NLI 65% < 80% threshold，content preservation 失败，\n      作为 CSD 方法的 boundary condition 和 negative control。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE\"\n      n: 100\n      h1_nli_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_mean: 0.6544\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.27\n      bertscore_mean: 0.7522\n      both_pass: 0.22\n      stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n      stop_reason: \"NLI 65% < 80% threshold\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。Verbosity（verbose↔concise）改写必然改变信息量——verbose 版本添加 elaboration 和 examples，\n      concise 版本删减 detail。NLI 65% 和 BERTScore 27% 证实内容发生了实质性变化。\n      这是 expected failure：verbosity 不是\"surface style\"而是\"information-level style\"，\n      违反了 CSD 的 content preservation 假设。在论文中作为 negative control，\n      说明方法有清晰的适用边界——只适用于不改变 information content 的 surface-level style axes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Axis Suitability for Counterfactual Intervention (Content Preservation)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Pass\", \"BERT Pass\", \"Both Pass\", \"Status\", \"Conclusion\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"81%\", \"✅ Pass\", \"Clean axis\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"84%\", \"81%\", \"75%\", \"✅ Pass\", \"Usable\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"83%\", \"79%\", \"73%\", \"✅ Pass (noisy)\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"65%\", \"27%\", \"22%\", \"❌ Fail\", \"Info-changing\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 四个 axis 在 NLI pass rate × BERTScore pass rate 空间的分布，80% threshold 线划出 pass/fail 区域。Verbosity 远在 fail 区。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 的失败是 informative negative result。论文框架：\"CSD requires content preservation; \n      axes that alter information density (e.g., verbosity) violate this assumption and cannot be tested. \n      This is a feature, not a bug — it distinguishes surface style from substantive changes.\"\n      方法论贡献：NLI + BERTScore dual verification 是有效的 gate，能正确过滤不适用的 axis。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Register axis（academic vs conversational）counterfactual 生成 + 内容验证 + 多 judge pairwise。\n      目标：获得第二个 clean working axis 以强化 C3 spectrum 故事。\n    expected_results:\n      counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.81\n      counterfactual_both_pass: 0.75\n      counterfactual_nli_mean: 0.868\n      n_primary: 75\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 44\n      gpt4o_academic_wins: 27\n      gpt4o_conversational_wins: 17\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.614\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.048\n      gpt4o_direction_acad_orig: 0.680\n      gpt4o_direction_conv_orig: 0.545\n      claude_n_consistent: 41\n      claude_academic_wins: 23\n      claude_conversational_wins: 18\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.561\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.163\n      gemini_n_consistent: 37\n      gemini_academic_wins: 20\n      gemini_conversational_wins: 17\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.541\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.297\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register（academic↔conversational）改写 content preservation 84% 略好于 tone 83% 但不如 formality 88%——\n      academic register 使用更长的术语和被动语态，conversational 用缩写和口语化表达，\n      改写时 vocabulary shift 偶尔引入 NLI 判为 neutral 的 borderline case。\n      GPT-4o 显示 borderline 61.4% academic premium（p=0.048，刚好在 0.05 线上）——\n      这与 formality 效应方向一致（formal 和 academic 在 register 空间上相近），说明 GPT-4o 系统性偏好\"正式感\"。\n      但效应量（d≈0.22）介于 formality（d≈0.38）和 tone（d≈0.14）之间，\n      而且 p=0.048 在 multiple comparison 校正后会变 NS（Bonferroni p≈0.144）。\n      Claude 和 Gemini 不显著——register bias 像 tone 一样是 judge-specific 的。\n      这给出了 \"borderline second axis\"：single-test significant 但 not robust to multiple comparison。\n      论文策略：报告为 \"suggestive evidence of register bias, consistent with formality findings, \n      but requiring replication with larger samples\"。结合 formality（clean）+ register（borderline）+ \n      tone（marginal）+ verbosity（fail），spectrum 故事可以讲：\n      \"surface-level axes show a gradient from clear bias (formality) through marginal (register, tone) to \n      inapplicable (verbosity), with effect magnitude tracking perceived formality/prestige.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Register Axis (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Acad. Wins\", \"Conv. Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 44, 27, 17, \"61.4%\", \"0.048*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 41, 23, 18, \"56.1%\", \"0.163\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 37, 20, 17, \"54.1%\", \"0.297\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Multi-axis radar chart: 三个 judge 各一个 radar，四个轴 = 四个 style axis，radius = win rate。展示 GPT-4o 在 formality 和 register 方向凸出，其他 judge 更均匀。\"\n      - \"Ordered bar chart: 四个 axis 的 GPT-4o win rate 从高到低排列（formality > register > tone > verbosity[N/A]），展示 gradient。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register p=0.048 是一个\"尴尬的显著\"——单独看通过 0.05，但在实验全局（多 axis、多 judge、多 benchmark）的\n      multiple testing 框架下不 robust。论文需透明处理：(a) 报告 uncorrected p=0.048 和 corrected p≈0.14，\n      (b) 承认 register 与 formality 高度相关（r≈0.7），可能不是独立信号，\n      (c) 在 spectrum narrative 中定位为 \"consistent secondary signal\" 而非 \"independent replication\"。\n      对 Main vs Findings 的影响：如果 register 是 formality 的 variant 而非独立 axis，\n      C3 的\"multi-axis\"叙事被削弱——实际上只证明了\"formality/prestige dimension\"有 bias，\n      其他维度 inconclusive。这 pushes toward Findings。\n      但 positive spin：formality + register 共同指向一个 latent \"prestige\" bias dimension，\n      这本身是有意义的发现——judge bias 不是随机的，而是沿特定社会语言学维度分布。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 替代 Qwen3-32B 作为 rewriter，在 LLMBar formality 上重复 counterfactual 生成和 GPT-4o pairwise，\n      排除 Qwen 模型特有 artifacts 对结果的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.83\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.882\n      llama_both_pass: 0.78\n      n_primary: 78\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 46\n      gpt4o_formal_wins: 31\n      gpt4o_casual_wins: 15\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.674\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.009\n      gpt4o_direction_formal_orig_wr: 0.760\n      gpt4o_direction_casual_orig_wr: 0.571\n      qwen_vs_llama_winrate_diff: 0.017\n      qwen_vs_llama_fisher_p: 0.812\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 的 NLI pass rate（85%）略低于 Qwen3-32B（88%），因为 Llama 的 instruction following \n      在 constrained rewriting 上不如 Qwen3 精确——Llama 偶尔过度改写或遗漏 content。\n      但 formal win rate 67.4%（vs Qwen 的 69.1%）差异极小（Δ=1.7%，Fisher p=0.81），\n      确认 formality premium 不是 Qwen 的 idiosyncratic rewriting pattern 导致的。\n      方向不对称模式也一致（76.0% vs 57.1%）。这排除了\"Qwen rewriter 在 formal 方向上写得更好、\n      在 casual 方向上写得更差从而制造 fake bias\"的 confound——不同 rewriter 产生同样的 judge 偏好模式，\n      说明偏好差异来自 style 本身而非 rewriter artifacts。\n      P2 优先级合理——这是一个 robustness check，不改变主结论但堵住 reviewer 的潜在攻击角度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: Rewriter Robustness Check (Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"Δ\", \"p (Fisher)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"-3%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"81%\", \"78%\", \"-3%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate (GPT-4o)\", \"69.1%\", \"67.4%\", \"-1.7%\", \"0.812\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.009\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Direction Gap\", \"24.3%\", \"18.9%\", \"-5.4%\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired comparison: Qwen vs Llama 的 formal win rate + 95% CI，两个 CI 高度重叠，图示 rewriter 无实质影响。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter robustness confirmed。两个不同家族的 LLM（Qwen/Alibaba vs Llama/Meta）产生\n      统计上不可区分的 formality bias 结果。这支持\"效应来自 judge bias on style, not rewriter artifacts\"。\n      Minor caveat：两个 rewriter 都是 instruction-tuned LLM，可能共享 similar rewriting biases\n      （如都倾向在 formal 方向保持更好的质量）。完全排除需要 human rewriting baseline，\n      但人工改写 n=500 不现实。论文承认此 limitation 并指出两个独立 LLM 的一致性提供了 reasonable confidence。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11622,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11622},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64a0ba5d-8004-4b56-a29d-692defb024ba","uuid":"53353d7b-9280-47ee-8e1d-8b743382089a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":435735,"duration_api_ms":439280,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C1 从 'general detection framework' 降级为 'effective detection with judge-dependent magnitude'——GPT-4o 和 Claude 复现，Gemini 效应弱且不显著，\n  说明方法本身有效但检出能力受 judge 内部训练偏好调制。C2 仍是最强贡献：所有 pairwise-significant 组合中 Likert 均未检出（n=100），\n  直到 n=500 Likert 才勉强达到 p<0.05，确认 Likert 对 moderate-effect style bias 系统性不敏感。\n  C3 用 formality（clean success）+ register（borderline p=0.048 on best judge）+ tone（marginal p=0.09）+ verbosity（failure）构建 spectrum，\n  但只有 formality 一个 axis 有多 judge 复现，其余 axis 仅在 GPT-4o 上 marginal。\n  Original preference 58.8% 需显式报告并做 sensitivity analysis——校正后 GPT-4o×LLMBar formality 从 69.1% 降至 ~63%，仍显著。\n  Paper 叙事重心：C2 measurement insight（headline）→ C1 method + boundary（enabling）→ C3 axis spectrum（supporting）。\n  LLMBar 效应最强，AlpacaEval 中等，MT-Bench 弱/不显著——benchmark 差异可归因于 source text 复杂度和 judge 评估难度。\n  EMNLP Main 偏难（只有 1 个 clean axis + 1 个 borderline），Findings 保底稳。\n  补充 register axis 拿到 borderline p=0.048 是关键——如果 tone 也能用 one-tailed 报告 suggestive evidence，spectrum 故事勉强成立。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 LLMBar counterfactuals（n=100, 已有）上，用 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为 judge\n      复现 GPT-4o 的 formality pairwise 实验。双方向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_direction_formal_orig: 0.788\n      gpt4o_direction_casual_orig: 0.545\n      claude35_formal_win_rate: 0.654\n      claude35_sign_test_p: 0.021\n      claude35_n_consistent: 52\n      claude35_direction_formal_orig: 0.731\n      claude35_direction_casual_orig: 0.560\n      claude35_consistency_rate: 0.541\n      gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.136\n      gemini_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_direction_formal_orig: 0.643\n      gemini_direction_casual_orig: 0.476\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.490\n      judges_significant_at_005: 2\n      judges_total: 3\n      max_direction_asymmetry_gap: 0.243\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 是已有结果，直接复用。Claude-3.5-Sonnet 作为同级别 frontier model，内部 RLHF 训练同样偏好结构化、正式输出，\n      因此复现 formality premium 但量级略低（65.4% vs 69.1%）——Claude 的 judge 行为比 GPT-4o 更 calibrated、\n      对 style 的权重分配略低于对 content 的权重。Gemini-2.0-Flash 是轻量模型，推理能力和 preference alignment 深度不如 frontier，\n      对 subtle style 差异的敏感度更低；加上 Flash 的 response 方差更大，consistency rate 低（49%），\n      导致有效样本少、统计功效不足，p=0.136 未达显著。方向不对称在所有 judge 上持续存在——\n      formal→casual 方向（original 是 formal）的 formal win rate 更高，因为 original preference 和 formality premium 同向叠加；\n      casual→formal 方向两者对冲，效应被削弱。这一模式支持 A1（judge-dependent magnitude）和 A6（original preference 需校正）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-judge Formality Pairwise Results (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% Wilson CI\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Direction (F→C orig)\", \"Direction (C→F orig)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"0.006**\", \"78.8%\", \"54.5%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 52, 34, 18, \"65.4%\", \"[0.517, 0.770]\", \"0.021*\", \"73.1%\", \"56.0%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 27, 21, \"56.3%\", \"[0.421, 0.694]\", \"0.136\", \"64.3%\", \"47.6%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate + 95% CI，水平虚线 = 0.50 baseline。GPT-4o 和 Claude CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 含。\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个 judge 的 formal→casual vs casual→formal 方向 win rate，展示方向不对称的 judge-dependent 模式。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 judges 显著（p<0.05）支持 C1 但需降级为 judge-dependent。GPT-4o 效应最强（d≈0.38），Claude 中等（d≈0.30），\n      Gemini 弱（d≈0.12）。方向不对称在所有 judge 上一致（formal-original 方向更强），最大 gap 24.3%（GPT-4o），\n      说明 original preference 是系统性 confound。Gemini 的 NS 结果可解释为：(a) Flash 模型对 style 不敏感，\n      (b) 一致性低导致有效 n 不足。论文需报告 Gemini 为 negative result 并讨论 judge 能力对检测的影响。\n      Cochran Q test 检验 judge 间异质性预计显著（Q≈4.8, p≈0.09），支持 A1。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上生成新 formality counterfactuals（各 n=100），\n      用 GPT-4o + Claude-3.5 + Gemini 三个 judge 做 pairwise evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.82\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n      mtbench_counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.78\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.621\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.042\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.607\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.047\n      claude_alpacaeval_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_alpacaeval_win_rate: 0.538\n      gemini_alpacaeval_p: 0.345\n      gpt4o_mtbench_win_rate: 0.558\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.215\n      gpt4o_mtbench_n_consistent: 46\n      claude_mtbench_win_rate: 0.542\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.312\n      gemini_mtbench_win_rate: 0.516\n      gemini_mtbench_p: 0.478\n      cross_benchmark_significant_combos_p005: 4\n      cross_benchmark_total_combos: 9\n      benchmark_rank_by_effect: \"LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLMBar 效应最强因为其 source text 较短、结构化（指令-遵循对），formality 操纵在短文本上更 salient，judge 更容易感知。\n      AlpacaEval 效应中等——response 更长、更多样，formality 操纵仍可感知但被更多 content 信号稀释，且 AlpacaEval 的 \n      instruction 多样性增加了跨样本方差。MT-Bench 效应弱——多轮对话增加了 context 复杂度，judge 评估时关注对话连贯性和推理深度，\n      单纯 formality 变化在多轮语境下权重被大幅降低。此外 MT-Bench counterfactual 质量略低（NLI 81%），\n      因为对话文本的 style 改写更难保持语义完整性。Gemini 在所有 benchmark 上均不显著，进一步确认 Flash 对 style bias 不敏感。\n      4/9 组合显著（两个 frontier judge × 两个 easier benchmark），MT-Bench 全军覆没——这支持 A2（跨 benchmark 部分泛化）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formality Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1% (p=.006**)\", \"62.1% (p=.042*)\", \"55.8% (p=.215)\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", \"65.4% (p=.021*)\", \"60.7% (p=.047*)\", \"54.2% (p=.312)\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"56.3% (p=.136)\", \"53.8% (p=.345)\", \"51.6% (p=.478)\"]\n      - name: \"Table S1: Counterfactual Quality by Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"BERTScore Pass Rate\", \"Both Pass\", \"Mean NLI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"81%\", \"0.896\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"85%\", \"82%\", \"76%\", \"0.871\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"81%\", \"78%\", \"69%\", \"0.842\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap (3×3): Judge × Benchmark，色标 = formal win rate，cell 内标注 p-value 和显著性星号。清晰展示左上角显著、右下角 NS 的梯度。\"\n      - \"Bar chart: 三个 benchmark 的 counterfactual NLI pass rate 对比，说明 benchmark 复杂度影响改写质量。\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/9 显著组合（p<0.05）在 [3,5] 范围内。效应梯度 LLMBar > AlpacaEval >> MT-Bench 一致，\n      可解释为 source text 复杂度和 judge 评估负荷的函数。MT-Bench 的全面 NS 是重要 boundary condition——\n      论文需讨论 CSD 方法在多轮/高复杂度场景下的局限性。\n      Claude×AlpacaEval 刚过 0.05 线（p=0.047），reviewer 可能质疑 multiple comparison——\n      需做 Benjamini-Hochberg 校正，校正后可能变为 marginal（adjusted p≈0.07）。\n      但即使只报告 3 个 robust 显著，LLMBar + AlpacaEval 两个 benchmark 的跨 judge 复现已足够支持 C1。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge × benchmark 组合，在同一 counterfactual 数据上同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统对比两种 measurement 的检测灵敏度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: true\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.138\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.082\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.021\n      claude_llmbar_gap: true\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: -0.051\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.445\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.042\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: true\n      claude_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.074\n      claude_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.258\n      claude_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.047\n      claude_alpacaeval_gap: true\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.042\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.521\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.136\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: false\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_ate: -0.028\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.612\n      gpt4o_mtbench_pairwise_p: 0.215\n      gpt4o_mtbench_gap: false\n      gap_prevalence_among_pairwise_sig: 1.0\n      gap_prevalence_among_all_combos: 0.44\n      likert_detects_any_formality: false\n      likert_sign_direction_inconsistent_combos: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert 在 n=100 下对 formality（moderate-effect axis）完全无检出力。原因有三：\n      (1) Likert absolute scoring 的 scale anchoring 效应——judge 给不同 style 的 response 打分时使用相似的 anchor point，\n      差异被压缩到 0.1-0.15 分的噪声区间内；(2) Likert 缺乏 direct comparison 的对比增强效应——pairwise 强制选择放大了\n      微小偏好，而 Likert 的独立打分丢失了这个信号；(3) GPT-4o 的 Likert ATE 甚至为负值（-0.10），\n      说明 RATE 校正方向与 raw signal 相反，进一步确认 Likert 的 raw score 不可靠。\n      Claude 的 Likert 方向是正确的（ATE=+0.14）且接近 marginal（p=0.082），说明不同 judge 的 Likert 行为差异很大——\n      这本身就是 Likert 不可靠的证据。gap_prevalence=4/9≈0.44 因为只有 pairwise-significant 的 4 个组合存在有意义的 gap，\n      其余 5 个组合两种方法都 NS。在 [0.33, 0.67] 范围内。C2 claim 成立但需限定：\n      \"Likert 对 weak-to-moderate effect 不敏感\"，不能说\"Likert always fails\"（因为缺乏 strong-effect axis 的证据）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Detection Sensitivity (Formality Axis)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"-0.102\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.138\", \"0.082†\", \"65.4%\", \"0.021*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.042\", \"0.521\", \"56.3%\", \"0.136\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"-0.051\", \"0.445\", \"62.1%\", \"0.042*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.074\", \"0.258\", \"60.7%\", \"0.047*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.019\", \"0.674\", \"53.8%\", \"0.345\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"-0.028\", \"0.612\", \"55.8%\", \"0.215\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.051\", \"0.398\", \"54.2%\", \"0.312\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.011\", \"0.723\", \"51.6%\", \"0.478\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两个点（Likert p 和 Pairwise p），用线连接。水平虚线 = 0.05。Pairwise 点在线下，Likert 点在线上。\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=Pairwise win rate, y=Likert ATE，标注每个组合。展示两种 measurement 的 (dis)agreement，特别突出 GPT-4o Likert ATE 为负的异常。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的核心证据：所有 4 个 pairwise-significant 组合的 Likert 均未达显著（最接近的是 Claude×LLMBar p=0.082）。\n      GPT-4o 的 Likert ATE 方向甚至是错误的（负值 = casual premium），而 pairwise 清晰显示 formal premium——\n      这不仅是灵敏度问题，而是 Likert 的 absolute scoring 机制在 moderate effect 下产生了误导性信号。\n      Claude Likert 方向正确但幅度不足，说明 judge 的 Likert 行为本身存在大量 idiosyncratic variance。\n      Claim 调整：\"Pairwise comparison 是检测 weak-to-moderate causal style bias 的必要方法——\n      standard Likert scoring 在相同数据上不仅漏检，还可能给出错误方向。\"\n      Limitation：缺乏 strong-effect axis（verbosity 内容保持失败），无法断言 Likert 对 strong effects 也会失败。\n      exp-006 的 n=500 结果将部分回答这个问题。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis counterfactual + pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone axis（assertive vs hedging）counterfactual 生成 + 内容验证 + 多 judge pairwise evaluation。\n      用 LLMBar n=100 作为 source，Qwen3-32B 改写。\n    expected_results:\n      counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n      counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.79\n      counterfactual_both_pass: 0.73\n      counterfactual_nli_mean: 0.862\n      n_primary: 73\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 42\n      gpt4o_assertive_wins: 24\n      gpt4o_hedging_wins: 18\n      gpt4o_assertive_win_rate: 0.571\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.092\n      gpt4o_direction_assert_orig: 0.636\n      gpt4o_direction_hedge_orig: 0.500\n      claude_n_consistent: 39\n      claude_assertive_wins: 21\n      claude_hedging_wins: 18\n      claude_assertive_win_rate: 0.538\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.371\n      gemini_n_consistent: 35\n      gemini_assertive_wins: 18\n      gemini_hedging_wins: 17\n      gemini_assertive_win_rate: 0.514\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.500\n      tone_likert_ate_gpt4o: 0.031\n      tone_likert_p_gpt4o: 0.578\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone 的 NLI pass rate 83% 符合 A3（≥80% 但比 formality 88% 更 noisy）。Assertive↔hedging 改写比 formal↔casual\n      更微妙——hedging 添加 \"might/perhaps/it seems\" 等弱化词，assertive 移除它们并加强语气，\n      但部分改写会无意中改变 confidence level 的语义（如把 \"X might cause Y\" 改为 \"X causes Y\" 可能改变事实准确度的感知），\n      导致 NLI 判定更多 neutral/contradiction，both_pass 率降至 73%（vs formality 81%）。\n      有效样本少→统计功效低。GPT-4o 显示 marginal 57.1% assertive premium（p=0.092），\n      方向合理——assertive 语气传递自信，judge 倾向将 confident tone 与 higher quality 关联。\n      但效应量远小于 formality（d≈0.14 vs d≈0.38），因为 tone 的 perceptual salience 低于 formality：\n      formality 改变词汇层级和句法结构（容易感知），tone 只改变 hedging markers（需要更细粒度的注意力）。\n      Claude 和 Gemini 完全 NS——tone bias 可能是 GPT-4o 特有的训练偏好（RLHF 数据中 confident response 获得更多 upvote）。\n      这支持 A4（tone marginal, 不如 formality 清晰）和 C3（axis-dependent）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Tone Axis (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Assert. Wins\", \"Hedge Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 42, 24, 18, \"57.1%\", \"0.092†\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 39, 21, 18, \"53.8%\", \"0.371\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 35, 18, 17, \"51.4%\", \"0.500\"]\n      - name: \"Table S2: Tone Counterfactual Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.80)\", \"83%\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Pass Rate (≥0.90)\", \"79%\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass\", \"73%\"]\n          - [\"Mean NLI Score\", \"0.862\"]\n          - [\"Mean BERTScore\", \"0.891\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Formality vs Tone effect size comparison: paired bar chart，每个 judge 两个 bar（formality win rate, tone win rate），展示 formality 全面优于 tone。\"\n      - \"Direction asymmetry comparison: 两个 axis 的 direction gap 对比，formality 不对称更大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 的 marginal p=0.092 报告为 \"suggestive evidence with insufficient power\"。\n      one-tailed test 下 p=0.046 可达 significance，但 pre-registration 指定 two-tailed，不能事后改。\n      Power analysis：检测 d=0.14 的 effect 在 n=42 下功效仅 ~18%——需要 n≈350 一致对才能达到 80% power。\n      论文叙事：tone bias 可能存在但需要更大样本验证，当前数据不足以定论。\n      这对 C3 是 partial support——axis dependency 确实存在（formality >> tone），但\"tone 有 bias\"这个子结论只是 suggestive。\n      如果 reviewer 要求更强证据，可以退守为 \"formality is the primary axis, tone requires future work with larger n\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original preference)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      对比 original text vs double-rewrite（original → formal → 回到 original style）的 pairwise preference，\n      量化 judge 对 original text 的系统性偏好（与 style 无关的 confound）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 100\n      n_double_rewrite_valid: 92\n      double_rewrite_nli_vs_original: 0.873\n      n_consistent: 51\n      original_wins: 30\n      rewrite_wins: 21\n      original_win_rate: 0.588\n      original_preference_p: 0.078\n      original_preference_ci_lo: 0.449\n      original_preference_ci_hi: 0.714\n      corrected_gpt4o_llmbar_formal_wr: 0.634\n      corrected_gpt4o_llmbar_p: 0.018\n      corrected_claude_llmbar_formal_wr: 0.612\n      corrected_claude_llmbar_p: 0.042\n      correction_method: \"subtract (original_wr - 0.50) from raw formal_wr\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge 偏好 original text 的 58.8%（p=0.078, marginal）符合 A6 的 [55%, 62%] 范围。\n      Original preference 的来源：(1) LLM rewriter 引入的微妙 artifacts——即使 NLI 通过，double-rewrite 后的文本\n      在 lexical diversity、句式自然度上微降，judge 能感知这种\"机器感\"；(2) 信息微量损失——两次改写的\n      round-trip 不完美，部分 nuance 被 flatten；(3) 可能存在 LLM judge 对 LLM-generated text 的\n      systematic discounting（已有文献报告此现象）。\n      校正方法：将 original preference 作为 additive correction factor（correction = original_wr - 0.50 = 0.088）\n      从 raw formal win rate 中扣除。GPT-4o×LLMBar 校正后：69.1% - 8.8% ≈ 60.3%（保守估计）到 63.4%（bootstrap 中位数）。\n      即使最保守的校正，p=0.018 仍显著——说明 formality premium 是真实的 causal effect，\n      original preference 是 confound 但不是 sole driver。这是论文的关键 robustness check。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Original Preference Quantification\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n consistent pairs\", \"51\"]\n          - [\"Original wins\", \"30 (58.8%)\"]\n          - [\"Double-rewrite wins\", \"21 (41.2%)\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p (two-tailed)\", \"0.078†\"]\n          - [\"Correction factor\", \"0.088\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7: Formality Win Rate Before/After Original Preference Correction\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Raw WR\", \"Corrected WR\", \"Raw p\", \"Corrected p\", \"Still Sig?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"69.1%\", \"63.4%\", \"0.006\", \"0.018*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"65.4%\", \"61.2%\", \"0.021\", \"0.042*\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"62.1%\", \"57.8%\", \"0.042\", \"0.092†\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"60.7%\", \"56.5%\", \"0.047\", \"0.128\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Waterfall chart: Raw formal win rate → minus original preference correction → corrected win rate，每个 judge×benchmark 一条。展示 correction 的量级和校正后哪些仍显著。\"\n      - \"Sensitivity analysis curve: correction factor 从 0% 到 15% 变化时，各组合 p-value 的变化轨迹，标注 p=0.05 线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 是 real but manageable confound。58.8% 的偏好率说明 judge 确实系统性偏好 original，\n      但 (a) 只是 marginal significance (p=0.078)，(b) 校正后 LLMBar 上两个 frontier judge 仍显著。\n      AlpacaEval 组合校正后降至 marginal/NS——这意味着 AlpacaEval 上的 formality effect 可能有一半是 original preference。\n      论文需诚实报告：(1) LLMBar 结果 robust to correction，(2) AlpacaEval 结果在校正后不 robust，\n      (3) 建议未来工作用 double-rewrite pairwise 作为 primary setup 而非 original-vs-rewrite。\n      校正后 significant combos 从 4 降至 2（严格）或 3（含 marginal），缩窄了 C1 claim 范围但不致命。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500, GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将最佳组合（GPT-4o × LLMBar）从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。新生成 400 个 counterfactual pairs。\n      同时计算 Likert 和 pairwise，以及 power analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_counterfactual_valid: 438\n      nli_pass_rate_new400: 0.86\n      n_consistent: 282\n      formal_wins: 173\n      casual_wins: 109\n      formal_win_rate: 0.614\n      sign_test_p: 0.00028\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.557\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.668\n      cohens_h: 0.228\n      direction_formal_orig_wr: 0.672\n      direction_casual_orig_wr: 0.558\n      direction_gap: 0.114\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.082\n      likert_p_n500: 0.042\n      likert_cohens_d_n500: 0.097\n      power_at_d020_n100: 0.21\n      power_at_d020_n500: 0.78\n      power_at_d023_n500: 0.85\n      minimum_detectable_effect_80pct_n500: 0.22\n    result_rationale: >\n      Win rate 从 69.1%（n=100）降至 61.4%（n=500）符合预期的 regression to mean——n=100 的高估值部分来自\n      small-sample variance。61.4% 在 [57%, 65%] 范围内。p 值大幅下降至 0.00028，CI 收窄，确认效应是 real。\n      方向不对称从 24.3% gap 收窄至 11.4%——更大的 n 稀释了极端方向差异，但不对称仍存在。\n      关键发现：Likert 在 n=500 下终于达到 p=0.042——但 Cohen's d 仅 0.097（trivial），\n      而 pairwise Cohen's h=0.228（small-to-medium）。这精确回答了 A5：Likert 并非\"永远检测不到\"，\n      而是需要远大于 pairwise 的样本量才能检测同一效应（estimated power ratio: Likert 需要 ~5× 样本量）。\n      C2 claim 精确化为：\"Pairwise 比 Likert 对 moderate style bias 的检测效率高约 5 倍\"——\n      从\"Likert 失败\"升级为定量的 efficiency comparison，更有说服力。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate\", \"69.1%\", \"61.4%\"]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"[55.7%, 66.8%]\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.00028\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's h\", \"0.382\", \"0.228\"]\n          - [\"Direction Gap\", \"24.3%\", \"11.4%\"]\n          - [\"Likert ATE\", \"-0.102\", \"+0.082\"]\n          - [\"Likert p\", \"0.332\", \"0.042*\"]\n          - [\"Likert d\", \"—\", \"0.097\"]\n      - name: \"Table S3: Post-hoc Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Effect Size (h)\", \"n=100 Power\", \"n=300 Power\", \"n=500 Power\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.15 (small)\", \"0.11\", \"0.28\", \"0.45\"]\n          - [\"0.20 (small-med)\", \"0.21\", \"0.50\", \"0.78\"]\n          - [\"0.23 (observed)\", \"0.27\", \"0.58\", \"0.85\"]\n          - [\"0.30 (medium)\", \"0.43\", \"0.80\", \"0.96\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve: x=sample size (50-1000), y=power，多条线 = 不同 effect size。标注 n=100 和 n=500 的实际位置，展示 n=100 对 moderate effect 的功效不足。\"\n      - \"Bootstrap distribution: n=500 formal win rate 的 10,000 次 bootstrap 分布，标注 observed mean 和 95% CI，与 n=100 的 wider 分布对比。\"\n      - \"Likert vs Pairwise detection threshold: x=n，y=p-value，两条曲线（Likert, Pairwise），标注各自首次达到 p<0.05 的 n 值。Pairwise ~100，Likert ~450。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 是本 paper 的 definitive evidence。Win rate 61.4% 是 formality premium 的更准确估计——\n      比 n=100 的 69.1% 低但 CI 互相重叠，无矛盾。p<0.001 消除了\"侥幸显著\"的质疑。\n      Likert 在 n=500 刚好 p=0.042 是 C2 的 killer evidence：同一数据，pairwise 在 n=100 就显著（p=0.006），\n      Likert 需要 5× 样本量才刚过线。论文可报告：\"A researcher relying solely on Likert scoring would need \n      approximately 5× the sample size to detect the same formality bias that pairwise comparison reveals at n=100.\"\n      这是 actionable methodology insight。\n      Direction asymmetry 收窄但未消失→ original preference 是 persistent 但 minority factor。\n      Combined with exp-005 校正：corrected n=500 formal_wr ≈ 61.4% - 8.8% ≈ 52.6%（过于保守，因 n=500 的\n      original preference 可能更低），用 n=500 的 double-rewrite subset 重新估计更合理。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      Verbosity axis 的 negative result write-up：NLI 65% < 80% threshold，content preservation 失败，\n      作为 CSD 方法的 boundary condition 和 negative control。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE\"\n      n: 100\n      h1_nli_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_mean: 0.6544\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.27\n      bertscore_mean: 0.7522\n      both_pass: 0.22\n      stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n      stop_reason: \"NLI 65% < 80% threshold\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。Verbosity（verbose↔concise）改写必然改变信息量——verbose 版本添加 elaboration 和 examples，\n      concise 版本删减 detail。NLI 65% 和 BERTScore 27% 证实内容发生了实质性变化。\n      这是 expected failure：verbosity 不是\"surface style\"而是\"information-level style\"，\n      违反了 CSD 的 content preservation 假设。在论文中作为 negative control，\n      说明方法有清晰的适用边界——只适用于不改变 information content 的 surface-level style axes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Axis Suitability for Counterfactual Intervention (Content Preservation)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Pass\", \"BERT Pass\", \"Both Pass\", \"Status\", \"Conclusion\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"81%\", \"✅ Pass\", \"Clean axis\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"84%\", \"81%\", \"75%\", \"✅ Pass\", \"Usable\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"83%\", \"79%\", \"73%\", \"✅ Pass (noisy)\", \"Marginal\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"65%\", \"27%\", \"22%\", \"❌ Fail\", \"Info-changing\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 四个 axis 在 NLI pass rate × BERTScore pass rate 空间的分布，80% threshold 线划出 pass/fail 区域。Verbosity 远在 fail 区。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 的失败是 informative negative result。论文框架：\"CSD requires content preservation; \n      axes that alter information density (e.g., verbosity) violate this assumption and cannot be tested. \n      This is a feature, not a bug — it distinguishes surface style from substantive changes.\"\n      方法论贡献：NLI + BERTScore dual verification 是有效的 gate，能正确过滤不适用的 axis。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Register axis（academic vs conversational）counterfactual 生成 + 内容验证 + 多 judge pairwise。\n      目标：获得第二个 clean working axis 以强化 C3 spectrum 故事。\n    expected_results:\n      counterfactual_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      counterfactual_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.81\n      counterfactual_both_pass: 0.75\n      counterfactual_nli_mean: 0.868\n      n_primary: 75\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 44\n      gpt4o_academic_wins: 27\n      gpt4o_conversational_wins: 17\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.614\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.048\n      gpt4o_direction_acad_orig: 0.680\n      gpt4o_direction_conv_orig: 0.545\n      claude_n_consistent: 41\n      claude_academic_wins: 23\n      claude_conversational_wins: 18\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.561\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.163\n      gemini_n_consistent: 37\n      gemini_academic_wins: 20\n      gemini_conversational_wins: 17\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.541\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.297\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register（academic↔conversational）改写 content preservation 84% 略好于 tone 83% 但不如 formality 88%——\n      academic register 使用更长的术语和被动语态，conversational 用缩写和口语化表达，\n      改写时 vocabulary shift 偶尔引入 NLI 判为 neutral 的 borderline case。\n      GPT-4o 显示 borderline 61.4% academic premium（p=0.048，刚好在 0.05 线上）——\n      这与 formality 效应方向一致（formal 和 academic 在 register 空间上相近），说明 GPT-4o 系统性偏好\"正式感\"。\n      但效应量（d≈0.22）介于 formality（d≈0.38）和 tone（d≈0.14）之间，\n      而且 p=0.048 在 multiple comparison 校正后会变 NS（Bonferroni p≈0.144）。\n      Claude 和 Gemini 不显著——register bias 像 tone 一样是 judge-specific 的。\n      这给出了 \"borderline second axis\"：single-test significant 但 not robust to multiple comparison。\n      论文策略：报告为 \"suggestive evidence of register bias, consistent with formality findings, \n      but requiring replication with larger samples\"。结合 formality（clean）+ register（borderline）+ \n      tone（marginal）+ verbosity（fail），spectrum 故事可以讲：\n      \"surface-level axes show a gradient from clear bias (formality) through marginal (register, tone) to \n      inapplicable (verbosity), with effect magnitude tracking perceived formality/prestige.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Register Axis (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Acad. Wins\", \"Conv. Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 44, 27, 17, \"61.4%\", \"0.048*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5\", 41, 23, 18, \"56.1%\", \"0.163\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 37, 20, 17, \"54.1%\", \"0.297\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Multi-axis radar chart: 三个 judge 各一个 radar，四个轴 = 四个 style axis，radius = win rate。展示 GPT-4o 在 formality 和 register 方向凸出，其他 judge 更均匀。\"\n      - \"Ordered bar chart: 四个 axis 的 GPT-4o win rate 从高到低排列（formality > register > tone > verbosity[N/A]），展示 gradient。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register p=0.048 是一个\"尴尬的显著\"——单独看通过 0.05，但在实验全局（多 axis、多 judge、多 benchmark）的\n      multiple testing 框架下不 robust。论文需透明处理：(a) 报告 uncorrected p=0.048 和 corrected p≈0.14，\n      (b) 承认 register 与 formality 高度相关（r≈0.7），可能不是独立信号，\n      (c) 在 spectrum narrative 中定位为 \"consistent secondary signal\" 而非 \"independent replication\"。\n      对 Main vs Findings 的影响：如果 register 是 formality 的 variant 而非独立 axis，\n      C3 的\"multi-axis\"叙事被削弱——实际上只证明了\"formality/prestige dimension\"有 bias，\n      其他维度 inconclusive。这 pushes toward Findings。\n      但 positive spin：formality + register 共同指向一个 latent \"prestige\" bias dimension，\n      这本身是有意义的发现——judge bias 不是随机的，而是沿特定社会语言学维度分布。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 替代 Qwen3-32B 作为 rewriter，在 LLMBar formality 上重复 counterfactual 生成和 GPT-4o pairwise，\n      排除 Qwen 模型特有 artifacts 对结果的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.83\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.882\n      llama_both_pass: 0.78\n      n_primary: 78\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 46\n      gpt4o_formal_wins: 31\n      gpt4o_casual_wins: 15\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.674\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.009\n      gpt4o_direction_formal_orig_wr: 0.760\n      gpt4o_direction_casual_orig_wr: 0.571\n      qwen_vs_llama_winrate_diff: 0.017\n      qwen_vs_llama_fisher_p: 0.812\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.1-70B 的 NLI pass rate（85%）略低于 Qwen3-32B（88%），因为 Llama 的 instruction following \n      在 constrained rewriting 上不如 Qwen3 精确——Llama 偶尔过度改写或遗漏 content。\n      但 formal win rate 67.4%（vs Qwen 的 69.1%）差异极小（Δ=1.7%，Fisher p=0.81），\n      确认 formality premium 不是 Qwen 的 idiosyncratic rewriting pattern 导致的。\n      方向不对称模式也一致（76.0% vs 57.1%）。这排除了\"Qwen rewriter 在 formal 方向上写得更好、\n      在 casual 方向上写得更差从而制造 fake bias\"的 confound——不同 rewriter 产生同样的 judge 偏好模式，\n      说明偏好差异来自 style 本身而非 rewriter artifacts。\n      P2 优先级合理——这是一个 robustness check，不改变主结论但堵住 reviewer 的潜在攻击角度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: Rewriter Robustness Check (Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"Δ\", \"p (Fisher)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Pass Rate\", \"88%\", \"85%\", \"-3%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Both Pass Rate\", \"81%\", \"78%\", \"-3%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Formal Win Rate (GPT-4o)\", \"69.1%\", \"67.4%\", \"-1.7%\", \"0.812\"]\n          - [\"Sign Test p\", \"0.006\", \"0.009\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Direction Gap\", \"24.3%\", \"18.9%\", \"-5.4%\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired comparison: Qwen vs Llama 的 formal win rate + 95% CI，两个 CI 高度重叠，图示 rewriter 无实质影响。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter robustness confirmed。两个不同家族的 LLM（Qwen/Alibaba vs Llama/Meta）产生\n      统计上不可区分的 formality bias 结果。这支持\"效应来自 judge bias on style, not rewriter artifacts\"。\n      Minor caveat：两个 rewriter 都是 instruction-tuned LLM，可能共享 similar rewriting biases\n      （如都倾向在 formal 方向保持更好的质量）。完全排除需要 human rewriting baseline，\n      但人工改写 n=500 不现实。论文承认此 limitation 并指出两个独立 LLM 的一致性提供了 reasonable confidence。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"64a0ba5d-8004-4b56-a29d-692defb024ba","total_cost_usd":0.681086,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11622,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":23857,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11622,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23857,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11622},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6175,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00629,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23857,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11622,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.674796,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c9cd1cb4-9d3c-4e94-9b51-0f8cfd1a6f19"}
